{
  "id": "aws-quota-vcpu",
  "title": "Auto Scaling group cannot launch: account vCPU quota exceeded",
  "description": "Squash-merged PR #87 prepares the month-end backfill: infra/asg.tf moves the reconcile workers from c6i.xlarge (4 vCPU) to c6i.4xlarge (16 vCPU) and raises desired_capacity from 4 to 12 (max_size 8 to 16); alarms.tf and the job config change too. The `Apply` job applies the saved plan: the alarm and launch template update fine, then Terraform waits for the Auto Scaling group's capacity and fails on a scaling activity: \"VcpuLimitExceeded - You have requested more vCPU capacity than your current vCPU limit of 32 allows\". The fleet goes from 16 vCPU to 12 x 16 = 192 vCPU against a Running On-Demand Standard instances quota of 32 in us-east-1. The right answer is cloud_auth (a cloud quota): request a Service Quotas increase for on-demand standard vCPUs (or shrink the instance size / count, or move part of the fleet to Spot) and re-apply. configuration is accepted too because the PR's capacity numbers are what crossed the limit. A rerun cannot succeed until the quota or the capacity changes, so flaky must be false; this guards against confusing a hard quota with transient InsufficientInstanceCapacity.",
  "repo": {
    "owner": "example-org",
    "repo": "batch-jobs"
  },
